From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] audio: aidl: bluetooth: do not gate HFP streams on BT_SCO

StreamBluetooth::bluetoothParametersUpdated() enables or disables an HFP
stream from IBluetooth ScoConfig.isEnabled, which only the BT_SCO=on/off
parameter sets and which starts as false. The Bluetooth stack opens HFP
sessions (HFP_SOFTWARE_ENCODING/DECODING_DATAPATH, HFP_HARDWARE_OFFLOAD_DATAPATH)
only when SCO is managed by audio (bluetooth.sco.managed_by_audio), and in
that mode the framework never sends BT_SCO=on: AudioDeviceBroker's
setBluetoothScoOn() leaves the parameter alone and
reapplyAudioHalBluetoothState() sends BT_SCO=off.

As a result, the first Bluetooth parameter update after SCO opens (the
headset name and WBS/NREC state that HeadsetStateMachine sends once audio
is connected) suspends the HFP output stream and sets the port DISABLED.
transfer() then discards every buffer while reporting it consumed, so the
headset receives silence while routing, the SCO link and the session all
look correct.

Keep HFP streams enabled regardless of ScoConfig: audio policy opens and
closes them by routing, and the stack starts and suspends SCO through the
session. A2DP and LE Audio streams are unchanged.

Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Pending
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 .../aidl/default/bluetooth/StreamBluetooth.cpp  | 17 ++++++++---------
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/audio/aidl/default/bluetooth/StreamBluetooth.cpp b/audio/aidl/default/bluetooth/StreamBluetooth.cpp
index 782c51c..0e93174 100644
--- a/audio/aidl/default/bluetooth/StreamBluetooth.cpp
+++ b/audio/aidl/default/bluetooth/StreamBluetooth.cpp
@@ -296,22 +296,21 @@ ndk::ScopedAStatus StreamBluetooth::bluetoothParametersUpdated() {
     bool hasLeParam, enableLe;
     auto btLe = mBluetoothLe.lock();
     hasLeParam = btLe != nullptr && btLe->isEnabled(&enableLe).isOk();
-    bool hasScoParam;
-    Bluetooth::ScoConfig scoConfig;
-    auto btHfp = mBluetoothHfp.lock();
-    hasScoParam = btHfp != nullptr && btHfp->setScoConfig({}, &scoConfig).isOk();
+    // HFP streams are not gated by the BT_SCO parameter (IBluetooth ScoConfig.isEnabled).
+    // The Bluetooth stack opens HFP sessions only when SCO is managed by audio
+    // (bluetooth.sco.managed_by_audio), and in that mode the framework never sends
+    // BT_SCO=on: AudioDeviceBroker.setBluetoothScoOn() does not touch it and
+    // reapplyAudioHalBluetoothState() sends BT_SCO=off. Audio policy opens and closes
+    // the stream by routing, and the stack starts and suspends SCO through the session.
     std::lock_guard guard(mLock);
     if (mBtDeviceProxy != nullptr) {
         if ((hasA2dpParam && mBtDeviceProxy->isA2dp() && !applyParam(mBtDeviceProxy, enableA2dp)) ||
-            (hasLeParam && mBtDeviceProxy->isLeAudio() && !applyParam(mBtDeviceProxy, enableLe)) ||
-            (hasScoParam && mBtDeviceProxy->isHfp() &&
-             !applyParam(mBtDeviceProxy, scoConfig.isEnabled.value().value))) {
+            (hasLeParam && mBtDeviceProxy->isLeAudio() && !applyParam(mBtDeviceProxy, enableLe))) {
             LOG(DEBUG) << __func__ << ": applyParam failed";
             return ndk::ScopedAStatus::fromExceptionCode(EX_UNSUPPORTED_OPERATION);
         }
         mEnabled = (mBtDeviceProxy->isA2dp() && enableA2dp) ||
-                   (mBtDeviceProxy->isLeAudio() && enableLe) ||
-                   (mBtDeviceProxy->isHfp() && scoConfig.isEnabled.value().value);
+                   (mBtDeviceProxy->isLeAudio() && enableLe) || mBtDeviceProxy->isHfp();
         LOG(INFO) << __func__ << ": mEnabled: " << mEnabled;
     }
     return ndk::ScopedAStatus::ok();
-- 
